      "problem": "Evaluate the polynomial $\\frac{{z}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{3z}{4}-\\frac{1}{2}$ at $z=2.$",
      "worked_solution": "To evaluate, we substitute $z=2$  into the polynomial and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{z}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{3z}{4}-\\frac{1}{2} & = \\\\ \\frac{{2}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{3(2)}{4}-\\frac{1}{2} & = \\\\ \\frac{4}{4}+\\frac{3}{2}-\\frac{1}{2} & = \\\\ 1+1 & = \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}\n$$",
